Hi all!

I'm installing a v210 with gentoo. Originally I compiled gentoo's
stable hardened 2.6.28 kernel package (which uses grsecurity), which
worked rather well.
Then I tried to upgrade the kernel to a fresh, grsecurity-patched 2.6.31.
This failed at the first boot, so I tried to see which part in this pile
introduces the bug. Eventually, I removed all nifty patches, and went
back to a plain vanilla 2.6.31.6 kernel, booted with nosmp.
And I still have the freeze, so that's why I'm here :)
(The .config came from the working 2.6.28 kernel, updated by make menuconfig)

The boot logs (good & bad) are attached, together with the .config file
of the new kernel built.

I'd appreciate any help to track down the problem.

Regards,
Laszlo

